cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this pipeline or its signal estimates, please cite it."
title: "FAERS-Pharmacovigilance: drug-substance safety signal detection in FAERS 2020-2024"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline over 20 quarters of the FDA Adverse Event Reporting
  System (8.74M report-versions deduplicated to 7.47M unique cases). Detects
  15 substances - including emerging ones such as xylazine, nitazenes,
  tianeptine and designer benzodiazepines - from structured report fields, and
  computes four disproportionality measures per drug-event pair (ROR, PRR,
  BCPNN information component, and an empirical-Bayes Gamma-Poisson EBGM).
  Adds substance-stratified ROR with a z-test on the log-ROR difference, so a
  signal can be assessed with and without substance co-mention.
type: software
